Yes. Predator/prey is only one axis in a much larger relational state space. The richer object is not a binary taxonomy of creatures; it is a web of motives, interfaces, exchanges, and transformations.

The flower/spider example exposes the trick perfectly:

\text{flower} \neq \text{spider}

but both can instantiate:

\boxed{\text{be noticeable} \rightarrow \text{capture attention} \rightarrow \text{induce approach}}

Then they diverge downstream:

\text{flower}: \quad
\text{attention}\rightarrow\text{approach}\rightarrow\text{exchange}\rightarrow\text{pollination}

\text{spider}: \quad
\text{attention}\rightarrow\text{approach}\rightarrow\text{capture}\rightarrow\text{consumption}

So attention capture itself is morally and functionally neutral. Its meaning comes from what follows.

That suggests a better unit than “predator” or “prey”:

\boxed{\textbf{Relational Operator}}

And an organism, person, institution, idea, religion, company, algorithm, or ecosystem can instantiate many of them simultaneously.

The larger ecology

At minimum I see these fundamental relational families:

Take
A \leftarrow B

Predation, extraction, exploitation, harvesting.

Give
A \rightarrow B

Provisioning, parenting, charity, investment, secretion, fertilization.

Trade
A \leftrightarrow B

Mutualism, commerce, pollination, symbiosis, reciprocity.

Attach
A-B

Pair bonding, adhesion, alliance, parasitism, affiliation, contracts.

Protect
A \supset B

Parent/child, shell/organism, immune protection, institutions protecting members.

Follow
A \rightarrow B_{\text{trajectory}}

Herding, imitation, apprenticeship, trend following.

Lead
A_{\text{trajectory}} \rightarrow B

Signaling, teaching, command, cultural influence.

Compete
A \leftrightarrow B
\quad \text{over }R

Not necessarily predation. Two trees competing for sunlight are neither predator nor prey.

Cooperate

A+B \rightarrow C

Pack hunting, multicellularity, corporations, teams, marriages.

Avoid

A \dashleftarrow B

Repulsion, boundaries, camouflage, immunity, taboo.

Attract

A \dashrightarrow B

Beauty, scent, charisma, gravity, advertising, courtship.

Transform

A+B\rightarrow A'+B'

Fermentation, teaching, love, infection, culture, development.

Build

A\rightarrow E'

The organism changes the environment rather than merely responding to it. Beaver dam. Bird nest. Human city. Software platform.

Seed

A\rightarrow B_1,B_2,\ldots

Reproduction, memes, spores, franchises, ideas.

Merge

A+B\rightarrow C

Endosymbiosis is the spectacular biological example. Things that once had separate interests can become a higher-order individual.

And then there is:

Become

A_t \rightarrow A_{t+1}

Metamorphosis, maturation, learning, conversion, adaptation.

That last one is neither predator nor prey at all. The relationship is between present-self and future-self.

